.Dd November 14, 2026
.Dt RAVEN-DOCTOR 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm raven-doctor
.Nd run ordered RavenBSD diagnostics
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -strict
.Op Fl -json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs the ordered checks of
.Pa architecture/17-modern-userland.md
section 3.4: required services and readiness, log writability, clock, root mount and free space,
.Pa /tmp
writability, network link and route, DNS, crash loops, configuration parse, log retention and
dropped counters, and an add-on inventory when present.
Each check is one object of
.Va kind :
.Dq check
with
.Va id ,
.Va status
.Pq Dq ok , Dq warn No or Dq fail ,
.Va detail
and an optional
.Va fix
text.
The fix is advice only; the command never runs it.
.Pp
The command exits 0 when no check fails.
Warnings do not fail unless
.Fl -strict
is given; a failed check exits 1.
If the doctor backend is unreachable it reports the error and prints no check objects.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr raven 1 ,
.Xr raven-status 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD modern userland contract, revision 1.
